        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Venice</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 421 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Traditionally on 25 March 421, with the dedication of the church of San Giacomo at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rialto">Rialto</a>; no surviving records deal with the founding, and the first settlers are held to have been refugees from Roman cities of the mainland</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a group of islands in the shallow Venetian Lagoon, between the mouths of the Po and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piave">Piave</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a> region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Republic of Venice and its doges; the Arsenal; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aldus-manutius">Aldus Manutius</a>; Venetian painting; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murano">Murano</a> glass; the Ghetto; the lagoon and its canals</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Venice is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a> region and of the Metropolitan City of Venice, and its lagoon and historic centre are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
